very l below 10.5666 - e.g. -1.791|c| at l = 2 - so the theorem's clause 'Every Hecke step increases the total weight' is false under its own stated E and true under the functional the proof actually uses. Note also that Part 1's 'changes the word length (from l to l-1)' is incomplete: the step yields two terms, of lengths l-1 AND l-2, as Part 3 itself then states. The clean repair is to drop the l(w) factor from the theorem's definition of E, which makes theorem, proof and monotonicity claim all consistent; the alternative (keep l(w)) requires rewriting Part 3 and abandoning the monotonicity clause.","history":3},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Institutional register.","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Clean.","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"No inflation.","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"No restating closer.","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Parts 1-3 are the three claims of the parent theorem.","history":2},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"uses-formal-coverage","group":"uses","result":"n/a","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","